t opens while driving can obstruct the driver's view and increase the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will either repair the hood latch striker, or replace the hood if necessary, free of charge.  Owner notification letters were mailed January 18, 2022.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is PBV.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":724826,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=21V932000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":9,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2016","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"19V298000","received":"2019-04-12","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"ENGINE AND ENGINE COOLING:ENGINE:GASOLINE:BELTS AND ASSOCIATED PULLEYS","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2018-2019 Acura MDX and Honda Pilot vehicles and 2019 Acura RLX, RLX Sport Hybrid, TLX and Honda Odyssey and Ridgeline vehicles.  The timing belt teeth may separate from the belt.","consequence":"Teeth separation from the timing belt may result in an engine stall, increasing the risk of crash.","remedy":"Honda will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the vehicle and replace any affected timing belt free of charge.  Vehicles receiving a replacement timing belt will also have the engine inspected and any damaged components will be replaced for free.   The recall began June 7, 2019.  Honda owners may contact customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's number for this recall is L4M.  Acura owners may contact customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Acura's number for this recall is Z4L.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":93946,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V298000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":9,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX HYBRID"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"18V221000","received":"2018-04-05","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"SEATS","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2018 Honda Pilot and Ridgeline vehicles and 2018 Acura MDX vehicles.  The front driver and passenger powered seats in the Honda vehicles and the driver powered seats in the Acura vehicles may have been assembled with improperly manufactured rivets.  In the event of a crash, the rivets can break causing the seats not to be secured to the floor.  As such, these vehicles may fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard (FMVSS) number 207, \"Seating Systems,\" and 210, \"Seat Belt Assembly Anchorages.\"","consequence":"In the event of a crash, if the seat does not remain secured to the floor, the seat occupant has an increased risk of injury.","remedy":"Honda will notify owners, and dealers will replace the driver seat frame assembly in Acura MDX vehicles, and replace the driver and front passenger seat slide rail frames in Honda Pilot and Ridgeline vehicles, free of charge.  The recall began May 30, 2018.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for this recall is D0S, and T0T.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":5810,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V221000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":3,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V751000","received":"2023-11-13","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"ENGINE AND ENGINE COOLING:ENGINE:HARD PARTS INTERNAL/MECHANICAL","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2015-2020 Acura TLX, 2016-2020 Acura MDX, 2016 and 2018-2019 Pilot, 2017 and 2019 Ridgeline, and 2018-2019 Odyssey vehicles.  Due to a manufacturing error, the connecting rod bearing in the engine may wear and seize, damaging the engine.","consequence":"A damaged engine may run improperly or stall while driving, increasing the risk of a fire, crash, or injury.","remedy":"Dealers will inspect and repair, or replace the engine as necessary, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed March 28, 2024. 2016-2017 Acura MDX owner letters were mailed November 1, 2024.  2016-2020 Acura MDX owner letters are expected to be mailed in mid-December 2024. Honda began mailing owner notification letters as of March 18, 2024. 2015-2016 Acura owner letters are expected to be mailed mid-December 2024, 2018 Acura TLX owner letters are expected to be mailed the end of March/early April 2024, 2019 Acura TLX owner letters are expected to be mailed mid-May 2024, 2020 Acura TLX owner letters are expected to be mailed mid-June 2024, and 2016-2020 Acura MDX owner letters are expected to be mailed January 27, 2025.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for these recalls are XG1 and GG0.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":248999,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V751000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":18,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2015","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2016","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2016","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2016","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2017","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2017","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2017","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"23V858000","received":"2023-12-19","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"FUEL SYSTEM, GASOLINE:DELIVERY:FUEL PUMP","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2013-2023 Honda Accord, Civic Coupe, Civic Sedan, Civic Hatchback, Civic Type R, CR-V, HR-V, Ridgeline, Odyssey, Acura ILX, MDX, MDX Hybrid, RDX, RLX, TLX, 2019-2022 Honda Insight, Passport, 2020 Honda CR-V Hybrid, 2018-2019 Honda Clarity PHEV, Fit, and 2015-2020 Honda Accord Hybrid, Pilot, Acura NSX vehicles.  The fuel pump inside the fuel tank may fail.","consequence":"Fuel pump failure can cause an engine stall while driving, increasing the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the fuel pump module, free of charge.  Owner letters were mailed September 6, 2024.  Owners may contact Honda customer service at 1-888-234-2138.  Honda's numbers for this recall are KGC and KGD.  This recall is an expansion of NHTSA recall numbers 21V-215 and 20V-314.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":2490460,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=23V858000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":107,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2018","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V"},{"year":"2018","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"RIDGELINE"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"FIT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ODYSSEY"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"RLX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"ILX"},{"year":"2019","make":"ACURA","model":"NSX"},{"year":"2019","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":true},{"campaign":"26V332000","received":"2026-05-22","manufacturer":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.)","component":"AIR BAGS:SENSOR:OCCUPANT CLASSIFICATION:FRONT PASSENGER","summary":"Honda (American Honda Motor Co.) is recalling certain 2018-2021, 2023 Acura TLX, 2019-2024 RDX, 2017-2020, 2022-2026 MDX, 2017-2021, 2023, 2025 Honda Ridgeline, 2017-2022 Pilot, 2019-2021 Passport, 2018-2026 Odyssey, 2019-2022 Insight, 2019-2021 HR-V, 2018-2020 Fit, 2020-2022 CR-V Hybrid, 2017-2022 CR-V, 2017-2018, 2021 Civic Type R, 2017-2021 Civic hatchback, 2016-2020 Civic coupe, 2016-2022 Civic, 2017-2022 Accord Hybrid, and 2016-2022 Accord vehicles. The front passenger seat weight sensor may crack and short circuit, which can cause the air bags to deploy unintentionally during a crash.","consequence":"Air bags that deploy unintentionally during a crash increase the risk of injury.","remedy":"Dealers will replace the seat weight sensors, free of charge. Owner notification letters were mailed July 7, 2026. Owners may contact Honda's customer service at 1-888-234-2138. Honda's numbers for this recall are BOL, WO9, OOA, WOM, XOH, NOC, POD, BOE, UOF, POB, EOG, AOI, QO8, TOJ, DO7, and SOK. This recall expands previous NHTSA recall number 24V064. Vehicle Identification Numbers (VINs) involved in this recall will be searchable on NHTSA.gov beginning May 29, 2026.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":98892,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=26V332000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":92,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"HR-V"},{"year":"2020","make":"ACURA","model":"MDX"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"ACCORD HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PILOT"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"PASSPORT"},{"year":"2020","make":"HONDA","model":"CR-V HYBRID"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"INSIGHT"},{"year":"2021","make":"ACURA","model":"TLX"},{"year":"2021","make":"HONDA","model":"CIVI